WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.282 --> 00:00:03.278
♪ [music] ♪

00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:08.568
Give me one minute and I'll show you
how BigQuery can help you

00:00:08.568 --> 00:00:10.631
get insights from your data, fast.

00:00:10.871 --> 00:00:13.356
BigQuery is Google Cloud's
enterprise data warehouse,

00:00:13.356 --> 00:00:17.011
designed to help you ingest, store,
analyze, and visualize data with ease.

00:00:17.486 --> 00:00:20.128
You can ingest data into BigQuery
by uploading in batch

00:00:20.458 --> 00:00:23.695
or by streaming data directly,
enabling real-time insights.

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:27.602
As a fully-managed data warehouse,
Google takes care of the infrastructure

00:00:27.602 --> 00:00:31.276
so you can focus on analyzing your data
up to petabyte scale.

00:00:31.977 --> 00:00:35.244
BigQuery supports a standard SQL dialect
that is ANSI compliant,

00:00:35.574 --> 00:00:37.975
so if you already know SQL,
you're all set.

00:00:38.315 --> 00:00:40.060
Interacting with BigQuery is easy.

00:00:40.060 --> 00:00:43.173
You can use the Cloud Console UI,
BigQuery command-line tool,

00:00:43.386 --> 00:00:45.923
or use the API with client libraries
of your choice.

00:00:46.749 --> 00:00:48.750
When it comes time to visualize your data,

00:00:48.750 --> 00:00:51.555
BigQuery integrates
with several business intelligence tools

00:00:51.555 --> 00:00:55.057
to help you turn complex data
into compelling stories.

00:00:55.676 --> 00:00:57.271
The pricing model is simple.

00:00:57.271 --> 00:01:00.686
You pay for data storage,
streaming inserts, and querying data.

00:01:01.341 --> 00:01:03.573
Loading and exporting data
are free of charge.

00:01:03.881 --> 00:01:06.360
Storage costs are based
on the amount of data stored.

00:01:06.668 --> 00:01:09.120
For queries, you can choose
to pay per query

00:01:09.120 --> 00:01:11.640
or a flat rate for dedicated resources.

00:01:11.870 --> 00:01:14.692
So next time you're looking
to analyze data, big or small,

00:01:14.692 --> 00:01:16.557
take a minute and look at BigQuery.

00:01:16.893 --> 00:01:20.456
To learn more, check out
<i>cloud.google.com/BigQuery</i>.

